# trait_type_reject.tkr — the §9.4 trait-is-not-a-dispatch-type REJECT channel. A trait in a match
# case and a trait in a generic constraint live one per namespace under src/; both are typing-stage
# rejections reported by the single failing build. They live apart from the collection-stage rejects
# (trait_mixin_reject), whose signature/collection errors would cut the item-body walk before these.

Feature: trait_type reject — a trait is not a dispatch type (§9.4)

  # (r2_match_case_trait) a trait names a match case, but a trait has no discriminant to test.
  Scenario: r2_match_case_trait — a trait in a match case is rejected
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "has no discriminant"

  # (r3_trait_in_constraint) a trait constrains a type parameter, but a trait is not a type.
  Scenario: r3_trait_in_constraint — a trait in a generic constraint is rejected
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "cannot appear in a constraint"
